    "---\n",
    "## 1. Complex Vector Spaces\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1.1 Definition\n",
    "\n",
    "A **complex vector space** $V$ over $\\mathbb{C}$ is a set equipped with two operations:\n",
    "- **Addition:** $|u\\rangle + |v\\rangle \\in V$ for all $|u\\rangle, |v\\rangle \\in V$\n",
    "- **Scalar multiplication:** $\\alpha |v\\rangle \\in V$ for all $\\alpha \\in \\mathbb{C}$, $|v\\rangle \\in V$\n",
    "\n",
    "satisfying 8 axioms (commutativity, associativity, identity, inverse for addition; compatibility, identity, distributivity for scalar multiplication).\n",
    "\n",
    "**The canonical example for quantum computing:** $V = \\mathbb{C}^n$, the set of all column vectors with $n$ complex entries.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1.2 Dirac Notation — Kets\n",
    "\n",
    "Dirac notation is the standard language of quantum mechanics. We write:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$|v\\rangle \\;\\equiv\\; \\text{a column vector (\"ket\")} \\in V$$\n",
    "\n",
    "For a qubit ($n=2$), the two standard basis vectors are:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}, \\qquad |1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "These are called the **computational basis** (or **standard basis**, or **$Z$-basis**).\n",
    "\n",
    "A general qubit state is a **superposition**:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha|0\\rangle + \\beta|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix} \\alpha \\\\ \\beta \\end{pmatrix}, \\qquad \\alpha, \\beta \\in \\mathbb{C}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ket-demo",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── 1. Computational basis kets ──────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "ket0 = np.array([[1],\n",
    "                 [0]], dtype=complex)   # |0⟩\n",
    "\n",
    "ket1 = np.array([[0],\n",
    "                 [1]], dtype=complex)   # |1⟩\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"|0⟩ =\", ket0.flatten())\n",
    "print(\"|1⟩ =\", ket1.flatten())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── 2. Superposition state |+⟩ = (|0⟩ + |1⟩) / √2 ──────────────────────────\n",
    "ket_plus = (ket0 + ket1) / np.sqrt(2)\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"|+⟩ = (|0⟩ + |1⟩)/√2 =\", ket_plus.flatten())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── 3. Another superposition ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "alpha = 1/np.sqrt(3)\n",
    "beta  = np.sqrt(2/3) * np.exp(1j * np.pi/4)   # complex amplitude with phase\n",
    "psi   = alpha * ket0 + beta * ket1\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"|ψ⟩ with α=1/√3, β=√(2/3)·e^{iπ/4}:\", psi.flatten())\n",
    "print(\"Norms squared: |α|²=\", abs(alpha)**2, \"|β|²=\", abs(beta)**2,\n",
    "      \"sum=\", abs(alpha)**2 + abs(beta)**2)"
   ]
