    "---\n",
    "## 2. Inner Product Spaces and Hilbert Spaces\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.1 Inner Product\n",
    "\n",
    "An **inner product** on a complex vector space $V$ is a map $\\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle : V \\times V \\to \\mathbb{C}$ satisfying:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Property | Statement |\n",
    "|----------|-----------|\n",
    "| Conjugate symmetry | $\\langle u, v \\rangle = \\overline{\\langle v, u \\rangle}$ |\n",
    "| Linearity in 2nd arg | $\\langle u, \\alpha v + \\beta w \\rangle = \\alpha \\langle u,v \\rangle + \\beta \\langle u,w \\rangle$ |\n",
    "| Positive definiteness | $\\langle v, v \\rangle \\geq 0$, with equality iff $v = 0$ |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Note on conventions:** Physicists (and Dirac notation) make the inner product **anti-linear in the first argument** and **linear in the second**. This is the opposite of the mathematician's convention. Always check which convention a source uses.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.2 Dirac Notation — Bras and Inner Products\n",
    "\n",
    "Given a ket $|v\\rangle$, its **dual vector** (bra) is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\langle v| \\;\\equiv\\; (|v\\rangle)^\\dagger = \\text{conjugate transpose (row vector)}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The **inner product** of $|u\\rangle$ and $|v\\rangle$ is written as a **bra-ket** (bracket):\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\langle u | v \\rangle \\;=\\; \\sum_{i} u_i^* \\, v_i$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This is just the standard Hermitian inner product on $\\mathbb{C}^n$.\n",
    "\n",
    "The **norm** of a vector is $\\||v\\rangle\\| = \\sqrt{\\langle v|v\\rangle}$.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.3 Hilbert Space\n",
    "\n",
    "A **Hilbert space** $\\mathcal{H}$ is a complex inner product space that is **complete** with respect to the norm induced by the inner product (i.e., every Cauchy sequence converges).\n",
    "\n",
    "**For finite-dimensional quantum computing:** any finite-dimensional complex inner product space is automatically complete, so $\\mathcal{H} = \\mathbb{C}^n$ for an $n$-dimensional system. Completeness matters for infinite-dimensional cases (continuous-variable systems, field theories).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Single qubit:** $\\mathcal{H} = \\mathbb{C}^2$\n",
    "\n",
    "**$n$ qubits:** $\\mathcal{H} = (\\mathbb{C}^2)^{\\otimes n} \\cong \\mathbb{C}^{2^n}$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "inner-product-demo",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Inner products and norms ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "def bra(ket):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Return the bra (conjugate transpose) of a ket.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return ket.conj().T\n",
    "\n",
    "def inner_product(u, v):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Compute ⟨u|v⟩ = u† v\"\"\"\n",
    "    return (bra(u) @ v).item()  # .item() extracts scalar from 1×1 matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "def norm(v):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Compute ||v|| = sqrt(⟨v|v⟩)\"\"\"\n",
    "    return np.sqrt(inner_product(v, v).real)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify orthonormality of computational basis\n",
    "print(\"=== Orthonormality of Computational Basis ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"⟨0|0⟩ = {inner_product(ket0, ket0):.4f}   (should be 1)\")\n",
    "print(f\"⟨1|1⟩ = {inner_product(ket1, ket1):.4f}   (should be 1)\")\n",
    "print(f\"⟨0|1⟩ = {inner_product(ket0, ket1):.4f}   (should be 0)\")\n",
    "print(f\"⟨1|0⟩ = {inner_product(ket1, ket0):.4f}   (should be 0)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"=== Norm of |+⟩ ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"‖|+⟩‖ = {norm(ket_plus):.6f}   (should be 1.0)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"=== Inner product ⟨0|+⟩ ===\")\n",
    "val = inner_product(ket0, ket_plus)\n",
    "print(f\"⟨0|+⟩ = {val:.6f}   (should be 1/√2 ≈ {1/np.sqrt(2):.6f})\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"=== Conjugate symmetry: ⟨u|v⟩ = conj(⟨v|u⟩) ===\")\n",
    "uv = inner_product(psi, ket_plus)\n",
    "vu = inner_product(ket_plus, psi)\n",
    "print(f\"⟨ψ|+⟩ = {uv:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"⟨+|ψ⟩ = {vu:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"conj(⟨+|ψ⟩) = {vu.conj():.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Equal? {np.isclose(uv, vu.conj())}\")"
   ]
