    "---\n",
    "## 3. Dirac Notation in Depth\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1 Outer Products and Operators\n",
    "\n",
    "While a bra-ket $\\langle u|v\\rangle$ is a **scalar**, a **ket-bra** $|u\\rangle\\langle v|$ is a **linear operator** (matrix) acting on $\\mathcal{H}$:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$(|u\\rangle\\langle v|)\\,|w\\rangle = |u\\rangle \\cdot \\langle v|w\\rangle = \\langle v|w\\rangle \\cdot |u\\rangle$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This is just a scalar ($\\langle v|w\\rangle$) times a vector ($|u\\rangle$).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Projection operators:** The operator $|v\\rangle\\langle v|$ (for a normalized $|v\\rangle$) is the **projector** onto the subspace spanned by $|v\\rangle$. It satisfies:\n",
    "- $P^2 = P$ (idempotent)\n",
    "- $P^\\dagger = P$ (Hermitian)\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.2 The Completeness (Resolution of Identity) Relation\n",
    "\n",
    "For any orthonormal basis $\\{|e_i\\rangle\\}$ of $\\mathcal{H}$:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\sum_{i} |e_i\\rangle\\langle e_i| = \\mathbb{I}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This is one of the most-used identities in quantum information — it lets you insert bases anywhere.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.3 Basis Expansion\n",
    "\n",
    "Using completeness, any state $|\\psi\\rangle$ expands as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$|\\psi\\rangle = \\mathbb{I}|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_i |e_i\\rangle\\langle e_i|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_i \\langle e_i|\\psi\\rangle \\, |e_i\\rangle$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The coefficients $\\langle e_i|\\psi\\rangle$ are the **components** of $|\\psi\\rangle$ in the basis $\\{|e_i\\rangle\\}$.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.4 Matrix Elements of Operators\n",
    "\n",
    "Given a linear operator $A: \\mathcal{H} \\to \\mathcal{H}$ and a basis $\\{|e_i\\rangle\\}$, the **matrix element** is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$A_{ij} = \\langle e_i | A | e_j \\rangle$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This completely determines $A$ in the chosen basis."
   ]
  },
