    "---\n",
    "## 4. Orthonormal Bases and Gram-Schmidt\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.1 Orthonormal Bases\n",
    "\n",
    "A set of vectors $\\{|e_i\\rangle\\}_{i=1}^n$ is **orthonormal** if:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\langle e_i | e_j \\rangle = \\delta_{ij}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $\\delta_{ij}$ is the Kronecker delta. An orthonormal set that **spans** $\\mathcal{H}$ is an **orthonormal basis (ONB)**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Common qubit ONBs:**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Z-basis (computational):**\n",
    "\n",
    "$$|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}, \\quad |1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**X-basis (Hadamard):**\n",
    "\n",
    "$$|+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}, \\quad |-\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Y-basis:**\n",
    "\n",
    "$$|i\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\i\\end{pmatrix}, \\quad |-i\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-i\\end{pmatrix}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.2 Gram-Schmidt Orthogonalization\n",
    "\n",
    "Given any basis $\\{|v_i\\rangle\\}$, Gram-Schmidt produces an ONB:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$|e_1\\rangle = \\frac{|v_1\\rangle}{\\||v_1\\rangle\\|}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$|u_k\\rangle = |v_k\\rangle - \\sum_{j=1}^{k-1} \\langle e_j|v_k\\rangle\\,|e_j\\rangle, \\qquad |e_k\\rangle = \\frac{|u_k\\rangle}{\\||u_k\\rangle\\|}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "gram-schmidt",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization ────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "def gram_schmidt(vecs):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization.\n",
    "    Input:  list of column vectors (numpy arrays shape (n,1))\n",
    "    Output: list of orthonormal column vectors\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    orth_basis = []\n",
    "    for v in vecs:\n",
    "        # Subtract projections onto already-computed basis vectors\n",
    "        u = v.copy().astype(complex)\n",
    "        for e in orth_basis:\n",
    "            u = u - inner_product(e, v) * e\n",
    "        # Normalize\n",
    "        n = norm(u)\n",
    "        if n < 1e-10:\n",
    "            raise ValueError(\"Input vectors are linearly dependent.\")\n",
    "        orth_basis.append(u / n)\n",
    "    return orth_basis\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Example: Start from a random non-orthogonal basis of C^3 ─────────────────\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "v1 = np.array([[1], [1], [0]], dtype=complex)\n",
    "v2 = np.array([[1], [0], [1]], dtype=complex)\n",
    "v3 = np.array([[0], [1], [1]], dtype=complex)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Input vectors (not orthonormal) ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"⟨v1|v2⟩ = {inner_product(v1, v2):.4f}  (non-zero ⟹ not orthogonal)\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "e_basis = gram_schmidt([v1, v2, v3])\n",
    "e1, e2, e3 = e_basis\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Gram-Schmidt ONB ===\")\n",
    "print(\"e1 =\", e1.flatten())\n",
    "print(\"e2 =\", e2.flatten())\n",
    "print(\"e3 =\", e3.flatten())\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"=== Orthonormality check ===\")\n",
    "for i, ei in enumerate(e_basis):\n",
    "    for j, ej in enumerate(e_basis):\n",
    "        val = inner_product(ei, ej)\n",
    "        print(f\"⟨e{i+1}|e{j+1}⟩ = {val.real:+.6f} {val.imag:+.6f}i\", end=\"  \")\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"=== Completeness check: Σ|ei⟩⟨ei| = I ===\")\n",
    "completeness = sum(outer(e, e) for e in e_basis)\n",
    "print(np.round(completeness.real, 6))\n",
    "print(\"Is identity?\", np.allclose(completeness, np.eye(3)))"
   ]
  },
