   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 5. Linear Operators on Hilbert Spaces\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.1 Linear Operators\n",
    "\n",
    "A map $A: \\mathcal{H} \\to \\mathcal{H}$ is **linear** if:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$A(\\alpha|u\\rangle + \\beta|v\\rangle) = \\alpha A|u\\rangle + \\beta A|v\\rangle$$\n",
    "\n",
    "In Dirac notation, the action of $A$ on $|v\\rangle$ is written $A|v\\rangle$.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.2 Adjoint (Hermitian Conjugate)\n",
    "\n",
    "The **adjoint** $A^\\dagger$ of an operator $A$ is defined by:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\langle u | A^\\dagger | v \\rangle = \\overline{\\langle v | A | u \\rangle} = \\langle Av | u\\rangle$$\n",
    "\n",
    "In matrix form: $A^\\dagger = (A^*)^T$ — conjugate transpose.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.3 Important Classes of Operators\n",
    "\n",
    "| Name | Condition | Physical meaning |\n",
    "|------|-----------|------------------|\n",
    "| Hermitian | $A^\\dagger = A$ | Observable (measurable quantity) |\n",
    "| Unitary | $U^\\dagger U = UU^\\dagger = I$ | Quantum gate, time evolution |\n",
    "| Projector | $P^2 = P = P^\\dagger$ | Measurement outcome |\n",
    "| Normal | $AA^\\dagger = A^\\dagger A$ | Diagonalizable in ONB |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key theorem (Spectral theorem):** Every normal operator on a finite-dimensional Hilbert space is diagonalizable in some ONB. Its eigenvalues are real if and only if it is Hermitian.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.4 Operator Norms and the Trace\n",
    "\n",
    "The **trace** of an operator is basis-independent:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\text{Tr}(A) = \\sum_i \\langle e_i | A | e_i \\rangle = \\sum_i A_{ii}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Key trace identities:\n",
    "- $\\text{Tr}(AB) = \\text{Tr}(BA)$ (cyclic property)\n",
    "- $\\text{Tr}(|u\\rangle\\langle v|) = \\langle v|u\\rangle$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "operators-demo",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Operators: Hermitian, Unitary, verification ───────────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pauli matrices\n",
    "I  = np.eye(2, dtype=complex)\n",
    "X  = np.array([[0, 1], [1, 0]], dtype=complex)   # σ_x\n",
    "Y  = np.array([[0,-1j],[1j,0]], dtype=complex)   # σ_y\n",
    "Z  = np.array([[1, 0], [0,-1]], dtype=complex)   # σ_z\n",
    "H  = np.array([[1, 1], [1,-1]], dtype=complex) / np.sqrt(2)  # Hadamard\n",
    "\n",
    "def is_hermitian(A, tol=1e-10):\n",
    "    return np.allclose(A, A.conj().T, atol=tol)\n",
    "\n",
    "def is_unitary(A, tol=1e-10):\n",
    "    return np.allclose(A.conj().T @ A, np.eye(A.shape[0]), atol=tol)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Properties of standard operators ===\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "header = f\"{'Operator':<12} {'Hermitian':<12} {'Unitary':<12} {'Trace':<10} {'Det':<10}\"\n",
    "print(header)\n",
    "print(\"-\" * len(header))\n",
    "\n",
    "ops = {\"I\": I, \"X (σx)\": X, \"Y (σy)\": Y, \"Z (σz)\": Z, \"H\": H}\n",
    "for name, op in ops.items():\n",
    "    herm = is_hermitian(op)\n",
    "    unit = is_unitary(op)\n",
    "    tr   = np.trace(op)\n",
    "    det  = np.linalg.det(op)\n",
    "    print(f\"{name:<12} {str(herm):<12} {str(unit):<12} {tr.real:<10.4f} {det.real:<10.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"=== Matrix elements of X in the Z-basis ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"⟨0|X|0⟩ = {(bra(ket0) @ X @ ket0).item():.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"⟨0|X|1⟩ = {(bra(ket0) @ X @ ket1).item():.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"⟨1|X|0⟩ = {(bra(ket1) @ X @ ket0).item():.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"⟨1|X|1⟩ = {(bra(ket1) @ X @ ket1).item():.4f}\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"=== Cyclic trace property: Tr(XY) = Tr(YX) ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"Tr(XY) = {np.trace(X @ Y):.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Tr(YX) = {np.trace(Y @ X):.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"=== Trace of outer product: Tr(|u⟩⟨v|) = ⟨v|u⟩ ===\")\n",
    "u, v = ket_plus, psi\n",
    "lhs = np.trace(outer(u, v))\n",
    "rhs = inner_product(v, u)\n",
    "print(f\"Tr(|+⟩⟨ψ|) = {lhs:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  ⟨ψ|+⟩   = {rhs:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Equal? {np.isclose(lhs, rhs)}\")"
   ]
