    "---\n",
    "## 6. Spectral Decomposition and Change of Basis\n",
    "\n",
    "### 6.1 Spectral Decomposition\n",
    "\n",
    "Every Hermitian operator $A$ on a finite-dimensional Hilbert space can be written:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$A = \\sum_i \\lambda_i |e_i\\rangle\\langle e_i|$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $\\{\\lambda_i\\}$ are its real eigenvalues and $\\{|e_i\\rangle\\}$ is the corresponding orthonormal eigenbasis. This is the **spectral decomposition** (or eigendecomposition) of $A$.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Consequence:** Any function $f(A)$ of a Hermitian operator is defined by:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$f(A) = \\sum_i f(\\lambda_i) |e_i\\rangle\\langle e_i|$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This is used constantly — for example, $e^{i\\theta A} = \\sum_i e^{i\\theta\\lambda_i}|e_i\\rangle\\langle e_i|$ defines unitary rotation gates.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 6.2 Change of Basis\n",
    "\n",
    "To express a state or operator in a different ONB $\\{|f_i\\rangle\\}$, use:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$U_{ij} = \\langle f_i | e_j \\rangle$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $U$ is a unitary matrix (the change-of-basis matrix). A state $|\\psi\\rangle$ has coordinates:\n",
    "- In $\\{|e_i\\rangle\\}$: $\\psi_i = \\langle e_i|\\psi\\rangle$\n",
    "- In $\\{|f_i\\rangle\\}$: $\\phi_i = \\langle f_i|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_j U_{ij}\\psi_j$"
   ]
  },
