    "\n",
    "A normalized qubit state $|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha|0\\rangle + \\beta|1\\rangle$ with $|\\alpha|^2 + |\\beta|^2 = 1$ lives on the **unit sphere in $\\mathbb{C}^2$**. But the physically distinct states (differing only by global phase are identified) correspond to points on the **Bloch sphere** — we'll study this fully on Day 6.\n",
    "\n",
    "For now, let's visualize the relationship between inner products and angles between states."
